There are a total of 44 invocations that the player can activate; each one increases the level of the raid as well as the player's loot potential at the end of the raid, affecting the player's quantity of loot and the chances of receiving the unique rewards.

For every 5 raid levels, enemy [[hitpoints]], defence, accuracy, and damage increase by 2% additively, with damage capping out at +150%. For example, a raid level of 100 will modify these stats for all enemies within the raid by +40%, whereas a raid level of 500 will modify enemy hitpoints, defence, and accuracy by +200%, and their damage by +150%. The formula is: 

<math> CalculatedStat = (BaseStat)(1 + RaidLevel/250) </math>

where ''CalculatedStat'' is capped at 150% when calculating for damage.

'''Note:''' The increased defence is a modifier on the enemy's ''[[Damage per second/Melee#Step six: Calculate the Defence roll|calculated defence roll]]'', not to the enemy's Defence level itself, while Defence-draining attacks such as the special attack from a [[Bandos godsword]] will drain the enemy's ''base Defence level''. This means that Defence-draining weapons are recommended to bring in to the raid, especially at higher raid levels. Keep in mind that different targets throughout the raid have various caps on Defence reduction (see their respective sections).

Boss invocations are listed in their respective section instead of here. In each boss section there is a recommendation whether or not the invocation should be toggled on in both solo and group settings. The recommendation assumes that the player has enough experience to do a run of level 400 or lower. Higher or specialized runs, such as level 540 raids or transmog raids require toggling less favourable invocations, which is likely to kill inexperienced players.

