'''Power''' or sometimes '''Chaos''' should be taken first for the smelling salts. They greatly increase damage, will result in less supplies being used overall, and typically the healing/prayer restoration brought into the raid should be enough to get through all paths. 

* If '''Dehydration''' is active, having [[Liquid adrenaline]] for P1 and P2 wardens is crucial, in order to use [[Keris partisan of the sun]] special attacks to heal.
** While still offered, [[Nectar]] and [[Ambrosia]] will not be able to be used.

For the second choice, take supplies you will find useful. Typically, choose life as the final fight will have loads of unavoidable chip damage. This decision could change if you died and lost boosts. Prioritise being boosted by salts and having enough supplies to heal through the damage. In team encounters, it can be useful to quickly coordinate what supplies people are offered/need.

===Path clearing===
The four paths can be cleared in any order. Unless the team is attempting specific boss challenges or combat achievements, the order should be as follows:

* Zebak > Kephri > Akkha > Ba-Ba - Done when learning the raid to avoid sudden deaths late into the raid from upset stomach or level 4 Zebak (assuming path level ups are on).
* Ba-Ba > Kephri > Akkha > Zebak - This format is more efficient, since the salt provides a greater boost to ranged and magic compared to melee. Ba-ba and Kephri are predominantly fought with melee, whereas Akkha and Zebak require a great deal more ranged and magic, with the former also needing a form of run energy restoration, which the salt provides. While kill times can exceed a single dose for both Akkha/Zebak and the Wardens, the stat boost persists even after the eight minutes expire; it just doesn't reapply itself. Using [[preserve]], one salt can be enough if used during Akkha (Akkha before Zebak is crucial for run energy regain) and Wardens.

If quiet prayers, walk the path, and at least path finder are turned on, starting Zebak is recommended in order to avoid excess chip damage in enrage phase.

While Walk the Path is active, switching Ba-Ba and Kephri will result in about a 0.07% increase in point total and will slightly reduce the time taken. However, as Apmeken is more dangerous than Scabaras, this is not recommended as a death in Apmeken will result in greater time loss.

Before entering the tombs, make sure to pre-pot as needed.

* If entering Zebak first, the player can drink a dose of super combat and ranging potion (divine can be used) if ranging, or a [[saturated heart]] if maging.
* If entering Ba-Ba first, pre-pot with a dose of '''divine''' super combat and '''normal''' ranging potion, a saturated or imbued heart, and overheal with one [[anglerfish]]. If a divine ranging potion is being used, the boost will likely wear off before the second set of boulders.

Once all four paths are cleared, the path to the Wardens will open.

==Path of Crondis==
===Challenge room===
To walk the Path of Crondis, players must fully grow the [[Palm of Resourcefulness]] in the centre of the room. The tree requires 175 units of water, with an additional 125 for every additional player in the raid.

Players must pick up the [[Water container (Tombs of Amascut)|water containers]] on the ground and fill them with the water from the [[Waterfall (Tombs of Amascut)|waterfalls]] in the room. The waterfalls are guarded by statues intent to prevent players from easily acquiring the water; the statues on the side launch long spikes in a retracting motion and the statue in front of the waterfall discharges poisonous clouds on the tiles in front of it that flow to the other end of the path. The poison only damages on the darker cloud; the lighter clouds serve as a warning to move out of the way. Getting hit by either of these traps will reduce any water in the container by 50% of its total amount, alongside lowering the player's Defence by 6, Agility by 3 and also two prayer points per hit.

After taking water from the waterfall, it will take time for it to recover, so players are advised to head to another waterfall to collect more water. In group encounters, the water will respawn accordingly to team size.

Periodically, [[Crocodile (Tombs of Amascut)|red crocodiles]] will also spawn from the corners of the room, whose number varies depending on the number of the players in the raid. If the palm is watered, they will focus on reducing it down in size. The crocodiles follow a unique aggression mechanic in which they prioritise the tree if it has been watered, then players carrying water, and finally players without any water as highest to lowest priority. While the crocodiles do not scale with raid level, they will always hit a max of 18 if they successfully hit that player. If the player in question had been hit by the spears or acid pools, an additional 3 damage is added for each hit to a maximum of 36. If [[Protect from Melee]] is active and the crocodile would have hit the player, the player will lose 12 prayer points and take 33% of the damage dealt. This will also reduce any water in the container by 50% much like getting hit by the traps. It takes ~40 seconds, after the challenge has been started, for first crocodiles to get to the palm. If player or group can carry enough water to the palm before that, they can safely ignore all crocodiles in the room. 

It is possible in solo encounters to complete the challenge without taking any damage in 34.8 or 32.4 seconds. This is done by walking through the gate right as player spawn in, picking up a northern water container and instantly running to the waterfall in the north-eastern corridor (importantly, player should make sure to run along the second most eastern row of tiles). Once player has filled the container, they click the palm to path to, and water it. As soon as player has watered the palm, they click the waterfall north-west. Again, as soon as water is collected, player clicks on the palm to deposit the water. 

This method will usually skip all damage using tile-skipping and due to the traps being on a sequence, which fits the timing. If player isn't confident about being on the right cycle, they can also manually dodge the poison clouds within 2 closest rows to the statues. If done right, no time is lost dodging. In order to achieve 32.4 seconds completion time, player must use the water container on palm and waterfalls, instead of left clicking them. This saves 1 tick on each interaction, for a total of {{Ticks|4}} timesave. 

Making use of run and tile-skipping (similar to avoiding wall beasts) can allow players to bypass most of the traps. The traps in each section follow a specific pattern which can be used to avoid damage. In order to skip all damage from spikes, player must start from one tile north or south of the first statue and then run past the statues without stopping. This also requires a moving start, meaning that in order to tile-skip a spike, player had to be moving continuously before arriving to start tile. Trying to tile-skip a spike after staying on a start tile for longer than 1 tick, will not work for the first spike.

